     These macros define data structures for different types of trees: splay
     trees and rank-balanced (wavl) trees.

     In the macro definitions, _T_Y_P_E is the name tag of a user defined struc‐
     ture that must contain a field of type _S_P_L_A_Y___E_N_T_R_Y, or _R_B___E_N_T_R_Y, named
     _E_N_T_R_Y_N_A_M_E.  The argument _H_E_A_D_N_A_M_E is the name tag of a user defined
     structure that must be declared using the macros SSPPLLAAYY__HHEEAADD(), or
     RRBB__HHEEAADD().  The argument _N_A_M_E has to be a unique name prefix for every
     tree that is defined.

     The function prototypes are declared with SSPPLLAAYY__PPRROOTTOOTTYYPPEE(),
     RRBB__PPRROOTTOOTTYYPPEE(), or RRBB__PPRROOTTOOTTYYPPEE__SSTTAATTIICC().  The function bodies are gener‐
